FitHub Phase 3 evidence — FR-13 dedicated workout-set rest time
Execution date: 2026-10-21 (Europe/Berlin)
Environment: Windows local development; Angular http://localhost:4041; ASP.NET Core http://127.0.0.1:5081; PostgreSQL development database plus Testcontainers PostgreSQL integration suite.
Test account: active-member@fithub.demo (synthetic active Member; no password recorded in this evidence file).

Concrete test data
- Workout: Free workout
- Exercise: Bench Press
- Repetitions: 8
- Weight: 60 kg
- Exercise duration: 45 seconds
- Rest: 90 seconds

Expected result
- Duration and rest use separate, visibly labelled fields and separate stored values.
- The completed session retains both values after refresh.
- Volume remains 8 x 60 kg = 480 kg.

Actual result
- Browser: the set preview displayed “8 reps × 60 kg · Duration 45 s · Rest 90 s”.
- Browser: after Save exercise, the completed-set table displayed Duration 45 s and Rest 90 s in separate columns; volume was 480 kg.
- Browser: after Complete workout and a full page refresh, the completed session still displayed Duration 45 s and Rest 90 s separately.
- PostgreSQL integration verification returned RestSeconds=90 from the persisted completed session and retained the 480 kg volume.
- Validation tests accepted null rest for historical rows and valid values, and rejected negative values and values above 3,600 seconds.

Decision: PASSED.
Build/test corroboration: backend unit 109/109; PostgreSQL integration 85/85; Angular 118/118; production build passed.
Related historical defect: DEF-005. Historical Phase 2 evidence remains unchanged.
